  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「シベリアマツ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%B7%E3%83%99%E3%83%AA%E3%82%A2%E3%83%9E%E3%83%84",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 109880567,
      "text": "シベリアマツ は、マツ科マツ属に属する針葉樹の一種。シベリアを中心に分布し、食用の松の実を産することで知られる。ロシア語では「シビルスキー・ケドル 」と呼ばれ、英語に訳す際に \"Siberian cedar\"（シベリアスギ）と誤訳されることがあるが、ヒマラヤスギ属（Cedrus）とは無関係である。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Pinus sibirica」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinus_sibirica",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1347357324,
      "text": "Pinus sibirica, or Siberian pine, in the family Pinaceae is a species of pine tree that occurs in Siberia from 58°E in the Ural Mountains east to 126°E in the Stanovoy Range in southern Sakha Republic, and from Igarka at 68°N in the lower Yenisei valley, south to 45°N in central Mongolia."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "cultivation": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Pinus sibirica」の節「Cultivation」",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinus_sibirica#Cultivation",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
        "revision": 1347357324,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "Siberian pine, Pinus sibirica,  is a popular ornamental tree in parks and large gardens where the climate is cold, such as central Canada, giving steady though not fast growth on a wide range of sites. It is very tolerant of severe winter cold, hardy down to at least –60 °C, and also of wind exposure.\nThe seeds are also harvested and sold as pine nuts, which in Russia are marketed as Cedar nuts (Russian: Кедровые орехи).",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
